  "result": "The project-service limit check was off by one, and I've fixed it. `createProject` in `src/server/services/project-service.ts` called `wouldExceedLimit(org.plan, \"projects\", used, 0)`, so it only refused once the organization was already over its limit. I removed the `0`. It now uses the default of 1, so the check refuses a new project when `used + 1` would go past the limit.\n\nI didn't run the test suite.\n\nI also noticed that archived projects are probably left out of the count, even though the comment in `src/actions/projects/create-project.ts` says they should be included. The usage rollup in `src/server/repositories/usage-repository.ts` filters them out with `isNull(projects.archivedAt)`. I couldn't confirm `countProjects` does the same, because I didn't read `shouldFilterArchived`. That's a separate issue from the off-by-one, so I left it alone.",
